      },
      "message": "fix(turning): stop reading thread valleys and neck steps as false hidden rest\n\nTwo geometric defects in the hidden-rest envelope scan blocked Profile Finish\n(and zero-leave Profile Rough) on a turned part with a neck and a modelled\nthread:\n\n1. In `solid_rest::crossings_from_claims`, bare boundary claims at one Z level\n   were merged only when coplanar. On a revolved mesh (e.g. 64 segments), a\n   column on a 45-degree meridian hits two non-coplanar tilted facets along\n   their shared edge and emitted two crossings instead of one, inverting\n   solid/air parity inside thread V-grooves and exposing the downward upper\n   flank as a hidden top (0.7028 mm false rest). Boundary claims now carry an\n   orientation-free CCW XY angular sector (keeping `Claim` at 40 bytes) so\n   non-coplanar bare-boundary groups settle by angular multiplicity: 1 for a\n   manifold seam, apex or rim, 0 for a grazing V-root or overhang fold.\n2. In `TurnedBand::excuses`, inflating the open recess `[p, roof]` by +/-reach\n   caused a pass ending right at a neck step (Z20..Z60) or starting at the\n   neck top (Z63..Z78) to claim the neck step face (0.2435 mm false rest) even\n   though no non-gouging tangent ball centre can sit outside the open recess\n   `(p, roof)`. `excuses` now checks strict entry into `(p, roof)`, while\n   passes that enter or bridge the recess still own its floor and convict.\n\nPinned by:\n- `solid_rest::tests::revolved_meridian_edge_and_v_root_keep_true_parity`\n- `scan_turned::tests::a_pass_stopping_at_a_neck_step_does_not_own_the_neck_recess`\n- `turned_hidden_rest::thread_valleys_and_neck_step_at_window_edge_are_not_false_rest`\n- `turning_hidden_floor::profile_finish_over_cone_neck_and_thread_posts`\n\nFixes #2880",
